hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24163","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to me, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, he said: While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a man of the people sneezed and I said: May Allah have mercy on you. The people stared at me, and I said: Woe to my mother, what is yours looking at me? He said: They began striking with their hands upon their thighs. When I saw them silencing me, I was silent. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed, may my father and mother be for him, I never saw a teacher before him nor after him better in teaching than him. By Allah, he did not rebuke me, revile me, nor strike me. He said: This prayer, nothing of people's speech is proper in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran, or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"24164","I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people newly covenanted with ignorance, and Allah has brought Islam, and among us are people who go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to them. I said: Among us are people who take omens. He said: That is something they find in their chests, so let it not turn them. I said: Among us are people who draw lines. He said: A prophet used to draw lines; whoever agrees with his line, that is it."
"24165","He said: I had a slave-girl herding sheep of mine toward Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah. I looked at her one day and the wolf had gone with a sheep of her sheep. I am a man from the children of Adam, I grieve as they grieve, but I struck her a blow. I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he deemed that grave upon me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not free her? He said: Bring her to me. I brought her to him. He said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer. And he said once: She is a believer, so free her."
"24166","Hashim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, things we used to do in ignorance: we used to go to soothsayers. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not go to soothsayers. He said: We used to take omens. He said: That is something one of you finds in himself, so let it not turn you."
"24167","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, and he was a companion, said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, have you seen matters we used to do in ignorance? We used to take omens. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is something one of you finds in himself, so let it not turn you. I said: We used to go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to soothsayers."
"24168","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam narrated to him three hadiths he memorized from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people newly covenanted with ignorance, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has brought Islam, and among us are men who draw lines. He said: A prophet of the prophets used to draw lines; whoever agrees with his line, that is it. He said: I said: Among us are men who take omens. He said: That is something they find in their chests, so let it not turn you. He said: I said: Among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to them. He said: This is a hadith."
"24169","He said: I had sheep in them a slave-girl of mine herding them toward Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah. I looked at them one day and found the wolf had gone from them with a sheep. I grieved, and I am a man from the children of Adam, I grieve as they grieve, and I struck her a blow. He said: That was grave upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not free her? He said: Call her. I called her. He said to her: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: She is a believer, so free her. He said: These are two hadiths."
"24170","He said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one day, and a man of the people sneezed and I said: May Allah have mercy on you. The people stared at me with their eyes, and I said: Woe to my mother, what is yours looking at me? He said: They struck with their hands upon their thighs. When I saw them silencing me I was silent, until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed. He called me. He said: May my father and mother be for him, I never saw a teacher before him nor after him better in teaching than him. He did not strike me, rebuke me, nor revile me, and said: This prayer, nothing of people's speech is proper in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran, or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. These are three hadiths he narrated to me."
"24171","Affan narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, he narrated to me this hadith similarly and added in it, and said: It is only glorification, magnification, praise, and recitation of the Quran, or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"24172","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah al-Sulami, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: A man of the people sneezed and I said: May Allah have mercy on you. The people stared at me, and I said: Woe to my mother, what is yours looking at me? He said: They began striking with their hands upon their thighs, and I knew they were silencing me, but I was silent. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the prayer, may my father and he be for him, he did not revile me, rebuke me, nor strike me, and said: This prayer, nothing of people's speech is proper in it; it is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Quran, or as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"24173","I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people newly covenanted with ignorance, and Allah has brought Islam, and among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to them. I said: Among us are men who take omens. He said: That is something they find in their chests, so let it not turn them. I said: Among us are men who draw lines. He said: A prophet of the prophets used to draw lines; whoever agrees with his line, that is it."
"24174","He said: While a slave-girl of mine was herding small sheep of mine toward Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah, I looked at her a look and the wolf had gone from them with a sheep. I am a man from the children of Adam, grieves as they grieve, but I struck her a blow. He said: That was grave upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: Shall I not free her? He said: Send to her. He said: He sent to her and he brought her. He said: Where is Allah? She said: In the heaven. He said: Who am I? She said: You are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"24175","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, that he said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Have you seen things we used to do in ignorance? We used to take omens. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is something you find in yourself, so let it not turn you. He said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to them."
"24176","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam, that the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who take omens. He said: That is something you find in yourselves, so let it not turn you. They said: Among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: Do not go to a soothsayer."
